{"metric":"robinson_trautman","source":[{"metric":"robinson_trautman","system":"axisymmetric","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters","ricci_tensor"],"version":"82f7ffb395faf079"},{"metric":"schwarzschild","system":"eddington_finkelstein_outgoing","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"8bfce6914f41a1cf"},{"metric":"schwarzschild","system":"spherical","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"31e1b848a0d0f510"}],"views":[{"id":"axis","label":"The axis","box":[-3.3916,2.8062,-1.8208,1.8208],"input":"The first front $f(0, \\theta)^2 = f_0^2\\left(1 - \\epsilon^2\\cos^2\\theta\\right)$ at $\\epsilon = 4/5$, with $f_0^2 = \\ln\\left((1 + \\epsilon)/(1 - \\epsilon)\\right)/(2\\epsilon)$ so that every front has the area $4\\pi r^2$, and after it the solution of the Robinson-Trautman equation, with the vacuum $2H = K - 2r\\,\\partial_u\\ln f - 2m/r$.","settings":"$m$ is the unit of every length and of $cu$.","restriction":"The axis of symmetry $\\theta = 0$ only, a totally geodesic surface, each point in the diagram a single event; off the axis the fronts have other curvatures and the lines of constant $r$ run otherwise.","caption":["The axis of symmetry of a Robinson-Trautman spacetime whose first wave front is prolate ($\\epsilon = 4/5$), each point in the diagram a single event. The outgoing rays, one for the pole of each wave front, are $p = \\arctan U$ with Kruskal's $U = -e^{-cu/4m}$, and an ingoing ray keeps the $V = (r/2m - 1)e^{(cu + 2r)/4m}$ it has once the fronts are round. The region the Robinson-Trautman equation reaches lies between the first front, $u = 0$, and $u = \\infty$, with the singularity $r = 0$ in its past and future null infinity along its upper edge.","The equation has no solution toward the past, so nothing lies before the first front: the spacetime has no past null infinity and no past event horizon. The fronts settle to round spheres, so $u = \\infty$ is the horizon $r = 2m$ of a Schwarzschild black hole. Joined across it to Schwarzschild's black hole and second exterior, as drawn here, the metric has five continuous derivatives in general. Until $cu = 1.18\\,m$ every line of constant $r$ on the axis is spacelike, since $g^{rr} < 0$ at every $r$ there, and from $cu = 4m$ on the lines are Schwarzschild's."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,-1.5708],[-1.5708,-1.5708],[1.5708,1.5708],[2.3562,0.7854]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,0.0],[-1.5708,1.5708],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,0.0],[-1.5708,-1.5708],[-3.1416,0.0],[-1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[0.0,-1.5708],[-1.5708,-1.5708],[1.5708,1.5708],[2.3562,0.7854]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[2.007,0.4362],[1.9369,0.3939],[1.8288,0.3429],[1.7447,0.3109],[1.6774,0.2947],[1.6263,0.2938],[1.5901,0.3053],[1.572,0.3184],[1.56,0.3318],[1.5406,0.3688],[1.5291,0.4106],[1.5208,0.4741],[1.5176,0.5514],[1.5184,0.657],[1.5349,1.0156],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[2.1971,0.6263],[2.16,0.6141],[2.1016,0.6052],[2.0503,0.6027],[2.0084,0.6069],[1.9737,0.6175],[1.9462,0.6331],[1.9232,0.6535],[1.9011,0.6817],[1.8768,0.7256],[1.8499,0.7906],[1.7171,1.1802],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[2.3109,0.7401],[2.2537,0.7573],[2.193,0.7871],[2.1434,0.8237],[2.0977,0.8695],[2.0334,0.9497],[1.8096,1.255],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[2.3503,0.7795],[2.253,0.8607],[2.1648,0.9454],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[2.356,0.7852],[1.5708,1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.0225,-1.5483],[-0.8458,-1.5583],[-1.5708,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.1377,-1.4331],[0.0591,-1.4483],[-0.0859,-1.4635],[-0.8466,-1.507],[-1.1483,-1.5313],[-1.5708,-1.5708]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.5318,-1.039]